    "title": "Hampton County administrator, Lavar Youmans, resigns - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ava Cartes No media credit provided. ,\n10 hours ago\nHAMPTON COUNTY, S.C. (WSAV) — The Hampton County Council announced it has accepted the resignation of county administrator Lavar Youmans.\nThe decision was made on April 24 at a council meeting. No comments were made about Youmans’ resignation at the meeting.\nWednesday is Youmans’ last day as county administrator. He was hired back on May 29, 2025.\nCouncil will ask the South Carolina Council Association of Counties and the Parker Poe law firm for suggested interim administrators.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WSAV-TV.\n1",
